Overview

Earned foundational IT certification validating core skills in hardware, software, networking, troubleshooting, and basic security principles.

Components

Certification | CompTIA A+
Focus Areas | Hardware, Networking, OS, Troubleshooting, Security
Level | Entry-Level IT Certification
Validation | Industry Standard Exam

Process

Studied and passed certification exams covering core IT domains including computer hardware, operating systems, networking fundamentals, troubleshooting methodologies, and basic security practices. Built foundational understanding of how systems operate from both user and administrative perspectives, supporting real-world IT support and infrastructure work.

Skills Learned
IT hardware fundamentals
Operating system concepts (Windows/Linux basics)
Networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP concepts)
Troubleshooting methodology
Basic cybersecurity principles
End-user support concepts
IT service workflow understanding
Structured technical problem solving
